# ==============================================================================
# comparative_saccharum
#
# This working directory is ~2.2 TB; the part worth versioning is ~1 MB of
# scripts, tables and notes. Without these rules a stray `git add .` tries to
# swallow the whole thing. Sizes noted below are as of 2026-08-09.
#
# Rule of thumb: track code, configuration, sample sheets and small result
# TABLES. Never track sequencing data, correlation matrices, edge lists, or
# anything an analysis script regenerates.
#
# NOTE: git does not support trailing comments on a pattern line -- a `#` after
# a pattern is part of the pattern. Keep every comment on its own line.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Bulk data trees ----------------------------------------------------------
# files/   1.2 T  correlation matrices, edge lists, networks, MI output,
#                 and the pearson_baseline/ archive
# raw_sugarcane/  277 G  Munoz raw reads
# run1/            81 G  nf-core/rnaseq output (salmon, dds)
# failed_sra_sugarcanedb/  5.7 G
# annotation/     299 M  eggNOG-mapper annotations for both references
files/
raw_sugarcane/
run1/
failed_sra_sugarcanedb/
annotation/

# china/ is 542 G of Kiet reads + nf-core output, but its sample sheets and
# nextflow config are small and describe the experiment -- keep those.
# Excluding china/** rather than china/ is deliberate: git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so `china/` + `!china/*.csv` silently
# does nothing. Subdirectories still match china/** and are pruned unvisited.
china/**
!china/*.csv
!china/*.config

# --- GET_TFS: keep the result tables, drop the heavy intermediates ------------
# The TF / MYB61 / module20 result TSVs total ~18 M and are read by the readout
# scripts, so they stay. The HMM databases and per-chunk search output do not.
GET_TFS/db/
GET_TFS/tf_reference/
GET_TFS/mytfdb/
**/chunks/
**/domtbl/
*.domtbl

# DIAMOND / MAFFT scratch caches (myb61 and module20 keep these under
# results/*/work) and any nextflow work directory.
work/

# --- Sequence and alignment files ---------------------------------------------
*.fa
*.faa
*.fna
*.fasta
*.pep
*.fa.gz
*.faa.gz
*.fna.gz
*.fasta.gz
*.pep.all.fa.gz
*.fastq
*.fq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.sam
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.dmnd
*.hmm

# --- Serialised R objects and other large binaries ----------------------------
# e.g. mcl_results_both_networks.rds is 8 G. If a small .rds is ever worth
# keeping, force it with `git add -f`.
*.rds
*.RData
*.rda

# --- Nextflow -----------------------------------------------------------------
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*
timeline*.html
report*.html
trace*.txt
dag*.html

# --- Reference PDFs and generated listings ------------------------------------
# Papers live at the repo root; figures under plots/ are committed deliberately.
# tree.txt is a 36 M generated directory listing.
*.pdf
!plots/**/*.pdf
tree.txt

# --- Language and editor junk -------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
*.Rout
.Renviron
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# LibreOffice/Excel lock files, left behind when a .tsv is opened in a GUI
.~lock.*#
